weekly visual diaries</a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p>working on a project that actually feels like multi-headed monster, but also thinking about monster as metaphor — for personifying that which we fear. I wrote about this a bit in <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/film-analysis-nope-2022-jordan-peele\" target=\"_blank\">a film review of Nope.</a> <br /><br />in drawing this, my subconscious was definitely inspired recently by <a href=\"https://www.lexymakesthings.com/portfolio\" target=\"_blank\">Lexy Ho-Tai</a>, an artist who joined my house on the webs course — and her beautiful fabric monster creatures. </p><p>and, my reoccuring urge to <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/monstera-jungle-snake-study\" target=\"_blank\">draw snakes</a>. <br /><br /><strong>the first sketch ~</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/dc7508e8-ca2a-43fd-b8e7-d0b9bca920f3/leviathan+hydra-1.25.25.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"2048\" height=\"2048\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/dc7508e8-ca2a-43fd-b8e7-d0b9bca920f3/leviathan+hydra-1.25.25.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/dc7508e8-ca2a-43fd-b8e7-d0b9bca920f3/leviathan+hydra-1.25.25.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/dc7508e8-ca2a-43fd-b8e7-d0b9bca920f3/leviathan+hydra-1.25.25.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/dc7508e8-ca2a-43fd-b8e7-d0b9bca920f3/leviathan+hydra-1.25.25.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/dc7508e8-ca2a-43fd-b8e7-d0b9bca920f3/leviathan+hydra-1.25.25.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/dc7508e8-ca2a-43fd-b8e7-d0b9bca920f3/leviathan+hydra-1.25.25.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/dc7508e8-ca2a-43fd-b8e7-d0b9bca920f3/leviathan+hydra-1.25.25.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  <p><strong><em>week of january 20-26, 2025</em></strong></p><p><em>deployment week for a year-long web project. it is a leviathan hydra monster that grows new heads everyday, challenging my control-freak perfectionism, in a phase (of the project) where I have zero control. K works at night while I sleep alone. I wake up to new heads. he dreams of code.</em> </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p>last week was: <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/three-waking-times\" target=\"_blank\">three waking times</a><br /><a href=\"https://keningonline.squarespace.com/visual-art\">more visual art</a><br />more on <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/creative-process\">creative process</a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n   ","author":"Kening Zhu","siteTitle":"kening zhu","siteHash":"ef8a94b9fc20c32a4ee7d94ee971337d278e8b2fafe747123e4eb5cea026e84e","entryHash":"b308adab5f1e2960f0364043cd15746ae00606d4c32d1aa0a91d709cbc183c75","category":"Sites"}